  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If VRC installed every mod ever to the game by default, menus would get overloaded with features they never use.  Not everyone wants the same features, but nobody wants their features left out.  This proposes a solution to that issue.  I think it is beneficial both for if VRChat does not allow client based coding at all, or if they do allow users to create their own code.\nThere could be an option to reboot the game to a plugin screen.  It restarts and gives a list of plugins and what they do.  You can select the plugins you want, and then hit a “continue with selected plugins” button.  It reboots again, this time with the plugins running.  \nThe only way to get to the plugins screen is a button in the menu, so it just boots into the game with whatever plugins you most recently selected when you launch from outside the game.  \nThis allows for end user feature customization while still maintaining that everything is run directly through VRChat.",
